<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Required for ATARU to appear as a calling option on a contact card, and for
    "Call ATARU" to work from Siri. INStartCallIntent donations silently do
    nothing without it.

    This entitlement needs a PAID Apple Developer Program membership. A free
    personal team cannot enable the Siri capability, and a device build that
    requests it fails to sign with a provisioning error.

    So this file is NOT applied by default. Opt in from Config.xcconfig:

        ATARU_ENTITLEMENTS = ATARU/Resources/ATARU.entitlements

    Leaving it unset keeps the app building and running exactly as before, with
    the contact-card entry as the only missing piece.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.developer.siri</key>
  <true/>

  <!--
    Push Notifications. ONE entitlement, covering both of ATARU's push paths:
    the PushKit VoIP push that rings the phone while the app is closed
    (VoIPPushService) and ordinary APNs notifications (RemotePushService,
    which replaced ntfy). Adding the second needed no entitlement change.

    "development" matches an Xcode-installed build and pairs with the SANDBOX
    APNs host; TestFlight and the App Store need "production" and the
    production host. Mismatching the two fails as BadDeviceToken and the push
    simply never arrives — see VoIPPushService.environment, which both
    services report to the server so it picks the right host.
  -->
  <key>aps-environment</key>
  <string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
